      "type": "text",
      "text": "Dopamine agonists (cabergoline, bromocriptine): less effective than somatostatin analogs; often used as adjuncts. Cabergoline is more potent than bromocriptine at lowering GH. Bromocriptine has been used in pregnant women w acromegaly without fetal harm."
     }
